\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Talk with us, Lord, Thyself reveal,
\par While here o'er earth we rove;
\par Speak to our hearts, and let us feel
\par The kindling  of Thy love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. With Thee conversing, we forget 
\par All time, and toil, and care;
\par Labour is rest, and pain is sweet,
\par If Thou, my God, art here.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Here then, my God, vouchsafe to stay,
\par And bid my heart rejoice;
\par My bounding heart shall own Thy sway,
\par And echo to Thy voice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thou callest me to seek Thy face;
\par 'Tis all I wish to seek,
\par To attend the whispers of Thy grace,
\par And hear Thee inly speak.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Let this my every hour employ,
\par Till I Thy glory see:
\par Enter into my Master's joy,
\par And find my heaven in Thee.
\par                                  Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

